      "spans": [
        {
          "id": "doc-ca3c249b3f5f::sentence-22",
          "documentId": "doc-ca3c249b3f5f",
          "text": "- In light of Russia’s full-scale invasion of Ukraine, which began in February 2022, Finland (together with Sweden) submitted its official letter of application to become a NATO Ally on 18 May.\n",
          "start": 1711,
          "end": 1905,
          "contextSpans": [],
          "context": "- In light of Russia’s full-scale invasion of Ukraine, which began in February 2022, Finland (together with Sweden) submitted its official letter of application to become a NATO Ally on 18 May."
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-ca3c249b3f5f::sentence-26",
          "documentId": "doc-ca3c249b3f5f",
          "text": "- On 4 April 2023, Finland became a full member of NATO, upon depositing its Instrument of Accession to the North Atlantic Treaty with the United States government during a ceremony at NATO Headquarters in Brussels.\n",
          "start": 2258,
          "end": 2474,
          "contextSpans": [],
          "context": "- On 4 April 2023, Finland became a full member of NATO, upon depositing its Instrument of Accession to the North Atlantic Treaty with the United States government during a ceremony at NATO Headquarters in Brussels."
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-ca3c249b3f5f::sentence-17",
          "documentId": "doc-ca3c249b3f5f",
          "text": "After almost 30 years of close partnership with NATO, Finland joined the Alliance on 4 April 2023. ",
          "start": 736,
          "end": 835,
          "contextSpans": [],
          "context": "After almost 30 years of close partnership with NATO, Finland joined the Alliance on 4 April 2023."
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-7a01f78ccd01::sentence-10",
          "documentId": "doc-7a01f78ccd01",
          "text": "Sweden became NATO’s newest member on Thursday (7 March 2024), upon depositing its instrument of accession to the North Atlantic Treaty with the Government of the United States in Washington DC. ",
          "start": 369,
          "end": 564,
          "contextSpans": [],
          "context": "Sweden became NATO’s newest member on Thursday (7 March 2024), upon depositing its instrument of accession to the North Atlantic Treaty with the Government of the United States in Washington DC."
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-7a01f78ccd01::sentence-12",
          "documentId": "doc-7a01f78ccd01",
          "text": "NATO Secretary General Jens Stoltenberg said: “This is a historic day. Sweden will now take its rightful place at NATO’s table, with an equal say in shaping NATO policies and decisions. After over 200 years of non-alignment Sweden now enjoys the protection granted under Article 5, the ultimate guarantee of Allies’ freedom and security. Sweden brings with it capable armed forces and a first-class defence industry. Sweden’s accession makes NATO stronger, Sweden safer and the whole Alliance more secure. Today’s accession demonstrates that NATO’s door remains open and that every nation has the right to choose its own path.”\n",
          "start": 637,
          "end": 1265,
          "contextSpans": [
            {
              "id": "doc-7a01f78ccd01::sentence-11",
              "documentId": "doc-7a01f78ccd01",
              "text": "With Sweden’s accession, NATO now counts 32 countries among its members.\n",
              "start": 564,
              "end": 637,
              "direction": "PREVIOUS"
            }
          ],
          "context": "With Sweden’s accession, NATO now counts 32 countries among its members. NATO Secretary General Jens Stoltenberg said: “This is a historic day. Sweden will now take its rightful place at NATO’s table, with an equal say in shaping NATO policies and decisions. After over 200 years of non-alignment Sweden now enjoys the protection granted under Article 5, the ultimate guarantee of Allies’ freedom and security. Sweden brings with it capable armed forces and a first-class defence industry. Sweden’s accession makes NATO stronger, Sweden safer and the whole Alliance more secure. Today’s accession demonstrates that NATO’s door remains open and that every nation has the right to choose its own path.”"
